{{!
    @template mod_edpreset/chooser_template_card

    One section template on the preset activities page: a whole section of the template course,
    offered as a single addable set.

    Deliberately carries data-templatesection rather than data-presetid. mod_edpreset/chooser parses
    data-presetid and then dereferences the card's select button without checking it exists, so a
    card with a preset id but no select button would throw the moment anything tried to select one.
    It does carry data-searchtext and data-tagkeys, because the filter walks every card in a group
    and reads both unguarded.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * templatesection int - section number in the template course; the template's identity
    * title string - the section name, with the [Template] marker already stripped
    * description string - already cleaned HTML of the section summary, rendered unescaped
    * icon string - pre-rendered icon HTML, taken from the section's first activity
    * modname string - the first activity's module, for the icon container
    * purpose string - the first activity's MOD_PURPOSE_*, which colours the icon
    * branded bool - whether the first activity's icon is branded and must not be recoloured
    * hasmultipletypes bool - the set spans more than one activity type, so the icon is drawn stacked
    * locked bool - a different template has already been used in this course, so this one cannot be
      chosen: the card is greyed out, its button disabled, and a note explaining why sits below it
    * modfullname string - the distinct activity types, e.g. "Book, Page, Quiz"
    * count int - how many activities the template adds
    * addurl string - a copy.php link carrying the template
    * searchtext string - lowercased title, description, activity types and tags, for the filter
    * tagkeys string - lowercased tags, pipe separated, for the in-page tag filter
    * hastags bool
    * tags array - name

    Example context (json):
    {
        "templatesection": 3,
        "title": "Weekly teaching cycle",
        "description": "<p>A prepare, engage, consolidate sequence for one week.</p>",
        "icon": "<img src='#' alt=''>",
        "modname": "book",
        "purpose": "content",
        "branded": false,
        "hasmultipletypes": true,
        "locked": false,
        "modfullname": "Book, Page, Quiz",
        "count": 4,
        "addurl": "https://moodle.local/mod/edpreset/copy.php?template=3",
        "searchtext": "weekly teaching cycle book page quiz",
        "tagkeys": "engage with content",
        "hastags": true,
        "tags": [{"name": "Engage with content"}]
    }
}}
{{!
    The card and its note are wrapped together so the pair occupies a single cell of the card grid,
    and so the filter - which toggles d-none on whatever carries data-region="card" - hides the note
    along with the card it explains rather than stranding it.
}}
<div class="edpreset-cardwrap"
     data-region="card"
     data-templatesection="{{templatesection}}"
     data-title="{{title}}"
     data-searchtext="{{searchtext}}"
     data-tagkeys="{{tagkeys}}"
>
<div class="card edpreset-card edpreset-template-card {{#locked}}edpreset-card-locked{{/locked}}">
    <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center mb-2">
            <h3 class="h6 mb-0 flex-grow-1 edpreset-card-title">{{title}}</h3>
            <span class="edpreset-tag edpreset-template-count ms-2">
                {{#str}} chooser:templatecount, mod_edpreset, {{count}} {{/str}}
            </span>
        </div>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center edpreset-modinfo edpreset-modinfo_{{modname}} mb-2">
            <div class="edpreset-card-icon icon-no-margin modicon_{{modname}} activityiconcontainer smaller {{purpose}} {{#branded}}isbranded{{/branded}} {{#hasmultipletypes}}edpreset-card-icon-stacked{{/hasmultipletypes}} me-1">
                {{{icon}}}
            </div>
            <small>{{modfullname}}</small>
        </div>

        <div class="edpreset-card-description flex-grow-1">{{{description}}}</div>

        {{#hastags}}
            <div class="edpreset-tags mt-2">
                {{#tags}}
                    <button type="button"
                            class="edpreset-tag"
                            data-action="tag"
                            data-tag="{{name}}"
                            aria-pressed="false"
                            aria-label="{{#str}} chooser:filterbytag, mod_edpreset, {{name}} {{/str}}"
                    >{{name}}</button>
                {{/tags}}
            </div>
        {{/hastags}}

        <div class="edpreset-card-actions d-flex align-items-center mt-3">
            {{#locked}}
                {{! A real disabled button rather than a styled-off link: an anchor cannot be
                    disabled, and copy.php refuses this template anyway - the button is the courtesy,
                    not the control. }}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm flex-grow-1" disabled>
                    <i class="icon fa fa-solid fa-ban fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{#str}} chooser:addtocourse, mod_edpreset {{/str}}
                </button>
            {{/locked}}
            {{^locked}}
                {{! An ordinary link, so a template can still be added with JavaScript off - it just
                    goes in as it stands, without the chance to interleave it with what is already
                    there. }}
                <a href="{{addurl}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm flex-grow-1" data-action="addtemplate">
                    {{#str}} chooser:addtocourse, mod_edpreset {{/str}}
                </a>
            {{/locked}}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{{#locked}}
    <div class="edpreset-card-note">{{#str}} templatelocked, mod_edpreset {{/str}}</div>
{{/locked}}
</div>
